TEXT 0 -200 Left 2 ;Lab A part 2a - driven by a PRESSURE source (1 Pa)
TEXT 0 -168 Left 2 ;IMPEDANCE analogy: node voltage = pressure [Pa], current = volume velocity [m3/s]. Narrow pipes = R_A + M_A in series, chambers = C_A to GROUND
TEXT 0 -136 Left 2 ;Vs1..Vs7 are 0 V sense sources: I(Vs7) is the volume velocity in the outlet pipe
TEXT 0 240 Left 2 !.param RA=25k MA1=2347.5 MA3=7512.1 MA5=9390.1 MA7=3756.1\n.param CA2=1.1249e-10 CA4=7.1995e-10 CA6=3.0373e-10
